## About the standard

Part 3-3 sets out technical security requirements for industrial automation and control systems. Asset owners and suppliers use it to specify the security capability a system needs.

The requirements are organized around seven foundational security areas, including identification, access control, system integrity, and availability. Security levels need to follow a system-specific risk assessment; the catalogue listing does not replace the standard.

Official source: [IEC 62443-3-3:2013](https://webstore.iec.ch/en/publication/7033).

